From 8e06817c69aa1e81d2f0513a548bee9957abc522 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:46:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information in the colours of the mark,
 clear of Estuary's bars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The player information of 1.0 did its work but looked like a default of
Estuary, and had faults that a look at it on a screen showed: it covered half
of the title and the clock above it and sat on the bar of the time; it was 900
px high whatever the page (some 210 px empty on the overview, half of the audio
and system pages); the tab of the page and the button "Change output for this
video..." were the same turquoise block, so that two things looked chosen at
once; rows behaved in two ways (some put their value on a second line under
the name), and one cut its text ("Γ.709"); each column had two headings, two of
them the same; the table of the metadata levels was "+" and "-" in text; the
speakers were turquoise blocks that looked like buttons.

Now, with every value of before still there:
- the panel stands between the title and the clock (to y 112) and the bar of
  the time (from y 960), and is as high as the page shown needs;
- its colours are those of the mark of LibreELEC Hades: the black of its tiles,
  the cold light of its rim on the panel's top edge and the warm point where
  the light breaks through at its start. The warm light marks only what matters
  now: the focus, a level that Hades uses, a value that just changed, a lit
  speaker;
- the focus is the one warm block; the tab of the page shown keeps a dark block
  when the focus is on the button; the button is a dark block until it has the
  focus, shown as Kodi shows a setting: "Output of this video" and, on its
  right, the output in use, with the key that does it, OK, before it;
- one model of row: name on the left, value on the right, from the same line;
  a long name or a long value takes a second line in its own cell (the room of
  the name is set per row where its texts need it). Every text was measured as
  Kodi measures it, in the four languages, with the battery's skin_check.py
  (19 labels and a column that did not fit at the first try; none now). The
  name of the composer row says "out" for "result" in English, as the Spanish
  already says "res.", so that it holds in two lines;
- one heading per column, its name in small bold capitals;
- the levels as dots, full where the level is there, hollow where it is not,
  the levels that Hades uses in the warm light; a legend says so;
- the speakers in a plan of the room seen from above: the screen at the top,
  the seat in the middle, the height speakers over the floor ones;
- the foot of the overview says how the machine is doing as values under their
  names.

The panel keeps what was decided for it: opaque, still while it is open (no
label of it moves; the values change twice a second at most), and smaller than
before (1760 x 766 on the overview against 1800 x 900). The dialog of
system/hades for other skins is made again from Estuary's files; it takes
Estuary's round button for the dots and no longer its square one.
